#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:299
msgid "Picomatch options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:301
msgid ""
"The following options may be used with the main `picomatch()` function or"
" any of the methods on the picomatch API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "**Option**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "**Type**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "**Default value**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "**Description**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`basename`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`boolean`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"If set, then patterns without slashes will be matched against the "
"basename of the path if it contains slashes.  For example, `a?b` would "
"match the path `/xyz/123/acb`, but not `/xyz/acb/123`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`bash`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Follow bash matching rules more strictly - disallows backslashes as "
"escape characters, and treats single stars as globstars (`**`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`capture`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`undefined`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Return regex matches in supporting methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`contains`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Allows glob to match any part of the given string(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`cwd`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`process.cwd()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Current working directory. Used by `picomatch.split()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`debug`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Debug regular expressions when an error is thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`dot`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Enable dotfile matching. By default, dotfiles are ignored unless a `.` is"
" explicitly defined in the pattern, or `options.dot` is true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`expandRange`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Custom function for expanding ranges in brace patterns, such as `{a..z}`."
" The function receives the range values as two arguments, and it must "
"return a string to be used in the generated regex. It's recommended that "
"returned strings be wrapped in parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`failglob`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Throws an error if no matches are found. Based on the bash option of the "
"same name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`fastpaths`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"To speed up processing, full parsing is skipped for a handful common glob"
" patterns. Disable this behavior by setting this option to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`flags`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Regex flags to use in the generated regex. If defined, the `nocase` "
"option will be overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "[format](#optionsformat)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Custom function for formatting the returned string. This is useful for "
"removing leading slashes, converting Windows paths to Posix paths, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`ignore`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`array|string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"One or more glob patterns for excluding strings that should not be "
"matched from the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`keepQuotes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Retain quotes in the generated regex, since quotes may also be used as an"
" alternative to backslashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`literalBrackets`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"When `true`, brackets in the glob pattern will be escaped so that only "
"literal brackets will be matched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`matchBase`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Alias for `basename`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`maxLength`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`number`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`65536`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Limit the max length of the input string. An error is thrown if the input"
" string is longer than this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`maxExtglobRecursion`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`number|boolean`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Limit nested quantified extglobs and other risky repeated extglob forms. "
"When the limit is exceeded, the extglob is treated as a literal string "
"instead of being compiled to regex. Set to `false` to disable this "
"safeguard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`nobrace`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Disable brace matching, so that `{a,b}` and `{1..3}` would be treated as "
"literal characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`nobracket`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Disable matching with regex brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`nocase`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Make matching case-insensitive. Equivalent to the regex `i` flag. Note "
"that this option is overridden by the `flags` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`nodupes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Deprecated, use `nounique` instead. This option will be removed in a "
"future major release. By default duplicates are removed. Disable "
"uniquification by setting this option to false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`noext`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Alias for `noextglob`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`noextglob`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Disable support for matching with extglobs (like `+(a|b)`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`noglobstar`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Disable support for matching nested directories with globstars (`**`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`nonegate`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Disable support for negating with leading `!`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`noquantifiers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Disable support for regex quantifiers (like `a{1,2}`) and treat them as "
"brace patterns to be expanded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "[onIgnore](#optionsonIgnore)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Function to be called on ignored items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "[onMatch](#optionsonMatch)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Function to be called on matched items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "[onResult](#optionsonResult)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Function to be called on all items, regardless of whether or not they are"
" matched or ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`posix`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Support POSIX character classes (\"posix brackets\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`posixSlashes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Convert all slashes in file paths to forward slashes. This does not "
"convert slashes in the glob pattern itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`prepend`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "String to prepend to the generated regex used for matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`regex`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Use regular expression rules for `+` (instead of matching literal `+`), "
"and for stars that follow closing parentheses or brackets (as in `)*` and"
" `]*`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`strictBrackets`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Throw an error if brackets, braces, or parens are imbalanced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`strictSlashes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "When true, picomatch won't match trailing slashes with single stars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`unescape`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Remove backslashes preceding escaped characters in the glob pattern. By "
"default, backslashes are retained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`unixify`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "Alias for `posixSlashes`, for backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:344
msgid ""
"picomatch has automatic detection for regex positive and negative "
"lookbehinds. If the pattern contains a negative lookbehind, you must be "
"using Node.js >= 8.10 or else picomatch will throw an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:346
msgid "Scan Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:348
msgid ""
"In addition to the main [picomatch options](#picomatch-options), the "
"following options may also be used with the [.scan](#scan) method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`tokens`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"When `true`, the returned object will include an array of tokens "
"(objects), representing each path \"segment\" in the scanned glob pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`parts`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"When `true`, the returned object will include an array of strings "
"representing each path \"segment\" in the scanned glob pattern. This is "
"automatically enabled when `options.tokens` is true"
msgstr ""

