#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:483
msgid "Basic globbing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "**Character**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Matches any character zero or more times, excluding path separators. Does"
" _not match_ path separators or hidden files or directories "
"(\"dotfiles\"), unless explicitly enabled by setting the `dot` option to "
"`true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`**`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Matches any character zero or more times, including path separators. Note"
" that `**` will only match path separators (`/`, and `\\\\` on Windows) "
"when they are the only characters in a path segment. Thus, `foo**/bar` is"
" equivalent to `foo*/bar`, and `foo/a**b/bar` is equivalent to "
"`foo/a*b/bar`, and _more than two_ consecutive stars in a glob path "
"segment are regarded as _a single star_. Thus, `foo/***/bar` is "
"equivalent to `foo/*/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`?`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Matches any character excluding path separators one time. Does _not "
"match_ path separators or leading dots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid "`[abc]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md
msgid ""
"Matches any characters inside the brackets. For example, `[abc]` would "
"match the characters `a`, `b` or `c`, and nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:492
msgid "Matching behavior vs. Bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:494
msgid ""
"Picomatch's matching features and expected results in unit tests are "
"based on Bash's unit tests and the Bash 4.3 specification, with the "
"following exceptions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:496
msgid ""
"Bash will match `foo/bar/baz` with `*`. Picomatch only matches nested "
"directories with `**`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/picomatch_README.md:497
msgid ""
"Bash greedily matches with negated extglobs. For example, Bash 4.3 says "
"that `!(foo)*` should match `foo` and `foobar`, since the trailing `*` "
"bracktracks to match the preceding pattern. This is very memory-"
"inefficient, and IMHO, also incorrect. Picomatch would return `false` for"
" both `foo` and `foobar`."
msgstr ""

